Z||000000||wkayl||04-26-2000||08:43 PM||||When taking my 14 year old daughter to school I have to drive about 15 blocks through residential area.  A little blue car drives the same route at about 10 to 15 mph.  Speed limit here is 25mph.  I have passed him (I checked with police and it is within the law if you don't go over the speed limit).  He tries to run into you when you pass, then he flips you off and tailgates.  Good thing my GT has enough pep to get out of his way.  He has done this 3 times to my car.  Now I drive my full size chev 4x4 and he still does it.  I called the cops and all they say is I can sign a complaint but it would be my word against his(he lives 1 block from me).  He also never stops at any stop signs (4 of them on this route).  I have given his plate number to the cops, but they never patroll this area to catch him.  <P>Any suggestions?  ||||reg||8
